ha-citrine source patch 0006 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27), applied after 0001 to 0005:
refuse a websocket upgrade with no charging station identity.

The station identity is the last segment of the upgrade URL path. A URL that
ends in "/" (the server root, or a trailing slash after the identity) gives
an empty identity, and nothing refused it: with unknown stations allowed, the
upgrade was accepted and created a ChargingStations row with an empty
ocppConnectionName. On the Green such a row, created during the Plugfest on
23 October, coincided with the 25 October heap exhaustions (ha-addons#80) and
broke Home Assistant discovery ("Missing or ambiguous station identity").
OCPP-J identifies the station by a non-empty identity in the URL path.

getClientIdFromUrl now throws UpgradeUnknownError for an empty identity, so
the upgrade is answered 404 like an unknown station, by every listener and
admission mode. Tests cover "/", "", a trailing slash and a root with a query.

diff --git a/packages/ocpp/src/transport/network-connection/util.ts b/packages/ocpp/src/transport/network-connection/util.ts
index b8f160dba..5ab5d23fd 100644
--- a/packages/ocpp/src/transport/network-connection/util.ts
+++ b/packages/ocpp/src/transport/network-connection/util.ts
@@ -11,11 +11,19 @@ import { UpgradeUnknownError } from './authenticator/errors/unknown-error.js';
  */
 export function getClientIdFromUrl(url: string): string {
   const pathSegment = url.split('?')[0].split('/').pop() as string;
+  let identifier: string;
   try {
-    return decodeURIComponent(pathSegment);
+    identifier = decodeURIComponent(pathSegment);
   } catch {
     throw new UpgradeUnknownError(`Unknown identifier ${pathSegment}`);
   }
+  // ha-citrine patch (0006-ocpp-empty-station-identity): a URL ending in "/" (the server root,
+  // or a trailing slash) has no station identity; OCPP-J requires one. Accepting it created a
+  // station with an empty ocppConnectionName.
+  if (identifier === '') {
+    throw new UpgradeUnknownError('Missing charging station identity in the URL path');
+  }
+  return identifier;
 }
 
